# Sentry Kubernetes Operator Acceptance Report

Status: REMEDIATION ACCEPTED LOCALLY AND ON SAAS; TEST TOKEN REVOCATION PENDING

Date: 2026-11-19

## Scope

This report records destructive acceptance testing performed only against disposable Sentry and
Kubernetes environments. A scenario is marked PASS only when the remote Sentry state, Kubernetes
resource status, and controller logs agree. Browser inspection is required for UI-visible fields.

The acceptance matrix covers:

- Sentry SaaS organization `test` (`test-pde`);
- self-hosted Sentry 26.10.1 with the feature-complete profile;
- self-hosted Sentry 24.7.1 with the legacy profile;
- all five public CRDs;
- create, update, pause/disable, adoption, fencing, retain, and deletion behavior;
- two controller replicas, ownership role transitions, and controller restarts;
- drift repair and credential failure/recovery;
- browser-visible Sentry settings and API-only fields documented by the runbook.

### Product-development investigation: notification integrations

The acceptance also investigates whether the operator should create or configure notification
integrations instead of only resolving an administrator-provided catalog. In Sentry SaaS, inspect
the complete Slack and PagerDuty setup flows and any other supported notification providers.
PagerDuty requires special attention: determine whether every PagerDuty service must still be
added manually, which objects are organization-wide versus service-specific, whether stable public
CRUD APIs exist, what credentials or OAuth hand-offs are required, and which lifecycle operations
can be owned safely. Record a proposed CRD or `SentryConnection` extension only after those API and
ownership boundaries are verified.

